figure out why unpacking is so much slower than PET (sometimes 10x slower!)
	- mrs extraction is the big bottleneck
	- approach one: memoization; most bits and pieces of MRS are reused many times
		- tried this on mrs_var's with good results, should also do ep's and hcon's
	- approach two: slab allocator; most of the time is spent in memory management
		- tried adding a cache of output property names, which good speedup
		- type names perhaps should be pointers to types, since much time is spent looking up and comparing types
		- should move to slab allocation for the rest of the mrs memory.
	- maybe some other aspects of unpacking are slow? not clear yet.

